# Terraform Provider for Docker Compose

[![Release](https://github.com/roshbhatia/terraform-provider-docker-compose/actions/workflows/release.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/roshbhatia/terraform-provider-docker-compose/actions/workflows/release.yml) [![Go Report Card](https://goreportcard.com/badge/github.com/roshbhatia/terraform-provider-docker-compose)](https://goreportcard.com/report/github.com/roshbhatia/terraform-provider-docker-compose)

This Terraform provider allows you to manage Docker Compose deployments on remote hosts over SSH.

## Features

- Deploy Docker Compose stacks to remote hosts
- Manage compose files and environment variables
- Support for SSH key-based authentication
- Container state tracking and health checks

## Usage

```hcl
terraform {
  required_providers {
    docker-compose = {
      source = "roshbhatia/docker-compose"
    }
  }
}

provider "docker-compose" {
  host        = "remote-host.example.com"
  user        = "deploy"
  private_key = file("~/.ssh/id_rsa")
}

resource "docker_compose_deployment" "app" {
  project_name = "myapp"
  compose_file = file("docker-compose.yml")

  environment = {
    APP_ENV = "production"
  }
}
```

## Development

### Requirements

- [Terraform](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/downloads) >= 1.0
- [Go](https://golang.org/doc/install) >= 1.21

### Building

```bash
make build
```

### Testing

```bash
make test
```
